Page No. 6 of 25 i. PW-1 Sona Devi who has inter-alia deposed about (i) head & fracture injury sustained by her brother Ravi in motor vehicle accident near Appu Ghar, Kapashera, New Delhi on 22.09.2018 at around 12:30 am (night) after TSR No.DL- 1RN-2510 was hit from behind by Maruti Wagon R Car No HR-46E-0122 driven at very high speed in rash and negligent manner as a result of which the TSR overturned and got dragged;
(ii) treatment at DDU Hospital & Safdarjung Hospital; (iii) expenses incurred on treatment,
medicines, conveyance, attendant charges & special diet;
(iv) monthly income Rs.20,000/- of Ravi Kumar by doing private job AND (v) general and special damages consequent to bodily injury sustained in road accident

. She has also relied upon - (a) copy of Aadhar Card of deponent - Ex.PW-1/1; (b) DAR - Ex.PW-1/2; (c) photocopy of Discharge Summary & OPD Record of Safdarjung Hospital - Ex.PW-1/3 (Colly.); (d) Original Bills filed along with Summary Chart - Ex.PW-1/4 (Colly.) ii.
PW-2 Sh. Shailender Kumar (injured in MACT No.1065/2018) who has inter-alia deposed about (i)
injuries sustained in the head and leg in motor vehicle accident near Appu Ghar, Kapashera, New Delhi on 22.09.2018 at around 12:30 am (night) after TSR No.DL-1RN-2510 was hit from behind by Maruti Wagon R Car No HR-46E-0122 driven at very high speed in rash and negligent manner as a result of which the TSR overturned and got dragged; (ii) treatment at DDU Hospital; (iii) expenses incurred on treatment, medicines, conveyance, attendant charges & special diet;

9. R3W1 Sh. Raj Kumar, Assistant, National Insurance Co. Ltd. has disputed liability of insurer to pay compensation in view of violation of the terms & conditions of Policy w.r.t. valid and effective licence for driving the vehicle by relying upon following documents:
 i. Authority Letter - Ex.R3W1/1;
 ii. Copy of Insurance Policy mentioning specific terms w.r.t. driving licence - Ex.R3W1/2;
iii. Copy of DAR, Charge-sheet, DL & Verification Report of RTO, Kushi Nagar Authority, Uttar Pradesh - Ex.R3W1/3.
Ravi vs Shiv Kumar on 2 May, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/197123513/
5 10.

Following factors are to be taken into account for assessing compensation under the head - Pain and Suffering:
 i. Nature of injury;
 ii. Parts of body where injuries occurred;
 iii. Surgeries, if any;
 iv. Confinement in hospital;
 v. Duration of the treatment.
